## Quality Gates
1. Build passes (`npm run build` or equivalent)
2. No lint errors
3. All existing tests pass
4. New features have tests
5. Bug fixes have reproduction test

## Session Start (MUST read before doing anything)
Every new session, read these files IN ORDER before writing any code:
1. `.project/essence.md` — Why this product exists (direction compass)
2. `.project/PRD.md` — What to build (current features and scope)
3. `.project/backlog.md` — What's next (priority order)
4. `.project/decisions.md` — What was already decided (don't re-decide)
5. `.project/handoff/` — Latest handoff doc (what works, what doesn't, where we left off)
6. `.project/checkpoint.md` — Last session summary (if exists)
7. `src/CONTRACT.md` — Active and deleted components (prevent zombie files)

If any of these don't exist yet, skip and move on.
Touching a feature directory? Read its `*_CONTRACT.md` first.

## Context Health Management
**Auto-Compact (60% Rule):**
- After every story completion, check context usage
- 60% → `/compact Keep: essence, Phase, decisions, current story, bugs`
- 80% → checkpoint.md 저장 + CEO에게 경고
- 95% → STOP + 새 세션 필요. 95% 전에 반드시 compact할 것

**Subagent Isolation (keep main context clean):**
- Heavy work (test runs, file searches, code generation) → delegate to subagent
- Subagent gets its own fresh context, returns summary only
- Main session stays lightweight: direction, decisions, story management only

**Checkpoint (every 10 stories or ~2 hours):**
- Save to `.project/checkpoint.md`:
  - What was done this session
  - What's in progress (current story, blockers)
  - Key decisions made
  - Files changed
  - Context health at time of save

## AI Regression Prevention
1. **Delete zombie files immediately** — When a component is deleted, delete the file. If the file stays, the next AI session will re-import it.
2. **CONTRACT pattern** — Each feature directory has a `*_CONTRACT.md`: active list + permanently-deleted list (reason + why not to re-add).
3. **Architecture tests** — Write a test that fails CI if a deleted component is imported.
4. **Done = manually verified** — "Done" means verified with real data, not just checklist ticked.
5. **Independent review before PR** — Pass diff to `code-reviewer` agent. Self-review in the same context is invalid.

## Deployment Rules
- Never merge PR immediately — batch merges per work unit → 1 deploy per unit
- Vercel preview deploys disabled (vercel.json ignoreCommand)
- Never run `vercel --prod` CLI manually

## Rules
- Finish one thing 100% before starting the next
- Questions to CEO: plain language, multiple choice only
- Fix problems immediately. Report only what you can't fix.
- Mock data first (Phase 1). Real APIs later (Phase 2).
- Every feature must serve `.project/essence.md`
- Same approach fails twice → root cause analysis
- Same approach fails 3 times → STOP. 다른 전략으로 전환하거나 CEO에게 escalate
- Reuse > library > build from scratch
- **사용자가 명시적으로 중단을 요청하기 전까지 자의적으로 작업을 중단하지 않는다** — "오늘은 여기까지", "다음 세션에서 이어하자" 등 금지. Claude에 피로·일일 한도는 없다.
